iZUgydmxnY0FDMGZ5bnhnNVZxWEhabUVlajVOelJyMXFhcWtWMVpPX055SXJNRjZnMmF2NHVPVkVEUGNVd1FLSWlDb0YxRGwxdzJsd0gwMEU2TGxNUQ?oc=5","date":"2026-10-20","zh":"為什麼 D.R. Horton (NYSE:DHI) 殖利率下滑近 5.1%？"},{"title":"Analysis: District 65 forensic report finds incomplete contract lists, inconsistent savings estimates","src":"Evanston RoundTable","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMihwFBVV95cUxNYUIzcnVDN0VtNUo4TExRdVhPai1jRFVEQV9PcGpGMXFCcno2cmdkUjNvUVpTSFcyaHpWSTJLOUxaNE1kY1hOczVmZklpZDZld0JHaTRnWUpsbkw2aUdYVU85VElvZG9QdEJ5MENtbGxkbG1jd3UxM3hvcWFKUk5rRGE0b2dQU28?oc=5","date":"2026-10-20","zh":"分析：第 65 區法證報告發現合約清單不完整，節省預算不一致"},{"title":"A Florida developer floated 864 apartments near Sarasota’s Celery Fields, then offered a 126-home settlem","src":"The Times of India","url":"https://news.google.?oc=5","date":"2026-10-20","zh":"佛羅裡達州開發商在薩拉索塔芹菜田附近建造了 864 套公寓，然後提供了 126 套住宅的定居點"},{"title":"D.R. Horton (NYSE:DHI) Stock Forecast & Analyst Predictions","src":"Simply Wall Street","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMigAFBVV95cUxQT1JvdVRHcjBzaEFRd2ZFWTd2RDk0T0RmR3RHTHZWSVVHYXZXZmpyWEZSdmQ0SmZhVHVRQndWNC1POVFTNHYxNmtMcTFJUnI5UDh1TzU5ZUc0VlBZUEdZM1FwemJjb0RpU2cwVE9Ld3VPLTEycjByckx2WXJLX3V3LQ?oc=5","date":"2026-10-19","zh":"博士霍頓 (NYSE:DHI) 股票預測和分析師預測"}],"themes":[{"name":"自駕/機器人","count":3},{"name":"訂單/合約","count":3},{"name":"財報","count":2},{"name":"分析師評等","count":2}],"biz":{"tenk":{"form":"10-K","date":"2025-11-19","period":"2025-09-30","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/882184/000088218425000081/dhi-20250930.htm"},"overview":[{"en":"D.R. Horton, Inc. is the largest homebuilding company in the United States as measured by number of homes closed. We construct and sell homes through our operating divisions in 126 markets across 36 states. Our common stock is included in the S&P 500 Index and listed on the New York Stock Exchange (NYSE) and NYSE Texas under the ticker symbol \"DHI.\" Our listing on NYSE Texas became effective in June 2025. Unless the context otherwise requires, the terms \"D.R. Horton,\" the \"Company,\" \"we\" and \"our\" used herein refer to D.R. Horton, Inc., a Delaware corporation, and its predecessors and subsidiaries.","zh":null},{"en":"Our homebuilding business began in 1978 in Fort Worth, Texas, and our common stock has been publicly traded since 1992. We have expanded and diversified our homebuilding operations geographically over the years by investing capital and building teams of people in our existing markets, starting new operations in additional markets and acquiring other homebuilding companies. We have closed more than 1.2 million homes during our 47-year history, and we have been the largest volume homebuilder in the United States every year since 2002.","zh":null},{"en":"Our business operations consist of homebuilding, rental, a majority-owned residential lot development company, financial services and other activities. Homebuilding is our core business, generating 92% of consolidated revenues of $34.3 billion and $36.8 billion in fiscal 2025 and 2024, respectively, and 90% of consolidated revenues of $35.5 billion in fiscal 2023. Most of our homebuilding revenue is generated from the sale of completed homes and to a lesser extent from the sale of land and lots. Approximately 84% of our home sales revenue in fiscal 2025 was generated from the sale of single-family detached homes, with the remainder from the sale of attached homes, such as townhomes and duplexes. Our product offerings include a broad range of homes for entry-level, move-up, active adult and luxury buyers. Our homes generally range in size from 1,000 to 4,000 square feet and in price from ","zh":null}],"markets":[],"customers":[],"competition":[{"en":"We operate as a provider of residential housing in both the for sale and rental markets, which are highly competitive. We compete not only for homebuyers and renters, but also for desirable properties, raw materials, skilled labor and financing. We compete with local, regional and national homebuilding and rental companies and also with existing home sales and rental properties. We compete based on price, location, quality and design of our homes and on mortgage financing terms.","zh":null},{"en":"Competition to our financial services businesses includes other mortgage lenders and title companies, including national, regional and local mortgage banks and other financial institutions. Some of these competitors are subject to fewer governmental regulations and have greater access to capital than we do, may operate with different lending criteria and/or may offer a broader or more attractive array of financing and other products and services to potential customers. We strive to provide flexible, fairly priced financing alternatives subject to applicable regulations.","zh":null}],"segments":{"seg":{"end":"2025-09-30","items":[{"name":"Home Building Ops","val":31515500000,"zh":"Home Building Ops"},{"name":"Forestar Group","val":1662400000,"zh":"Forestar Group"},{"name":"Rental","val":1640400000,"zh":"Rental"},{"name":"Financial Services","val":841200000,"zh":"Financial Services"}],"total":34250400000},"prod":{"end":"2025-09-30","items":[{"name":"Home Building Ops","val":31432000000,"zh":"Home Building Ops"},{"name":"Rental","val":1640400000,"zh":"Rental"},{"name":"Financial Services","val":841200000,"zh":"Financial Services"},{"name":"Land","val":336800000,"zh":"Land"}],"total":34250400000}},"peers":["LEN","PHM","TOL","KBH","BZH"]}}